   "title": "How much unsupported citations rose, on three models.",
   "takeaway": "The authors' model gives 2.19 for function and 2.84 for structure, and only structure's interval stays above 1. Weighted by citations the ratios drop to 1.77 and 1.54 and both intervals include 1. Inside single studies the rate rose 3.0 and 3.5 times.",
   "units": "ratio of the fitted rate of unsupported citations in the last year of a group's span to the rate in its first year. 1 is no change, 2 is a doubling.",
   "n": "268 study-year rates from 11 function and 7 structure focal studies",
   "interval": "95% interval from resampling focal studies. The within-study model has none in the run.",
   "series_names": [
    "network function",
    "network structure"
   ],
   "baseline": "Years shuffled inside each study, 1000 times, authors' model: 95th percentile 1.31 for function and 2.09 for structure. Both real ratios are above it, p 0.002 and 0.013.",
